165
00:04:29,430 --> 00:04:30,720
That friction is where

166
00:04:30,760 --> 00:04:32,390
a child learns to wait,

167
00:04:32,430 --> 00:04:34,760
to say sorry, to be counted on.

168
00:04:35,100 --> 00:04:36,400
A superintelligence can

169
00:04:36,440 --> 00:04:37,990
do your child's homework.

170
00:04:38,240 --> 00:04:40,370
It can't do any of that for them.

171
00:04:41,010 --> 00:04:43,350
Some economists expect a shift.

172
00:04:43,630 --> 00:04:45,720
When machines make answers cheap,

173
00:04:45,790 --> 00:04:46,900
what stays scarce

174
00:04:46,940 --> 00:04:48,810
is a person you can trust.

175
00:04:49,930 --> 00:04:51,210
But a shift like that should

176
00:04:51,250 --> 00:04:52,780
lift every child,

177
00:04:52,880 --> 00:04:54,480
not just a lucky few.

178
00:04:54,820 --> 00:04:55,860
This channel exists

179
00:04:55,900 --> 00:04:57,120
for one reason:

180
00:04:57,270 --> 00:04:58,130
so that the arrival

181
00:04:58,170 --> 00:04:59,370
of superintelligence

182
00:04:59,410 --> 00:05:01,170
