199
00:05:31,360 --> 00:05:32,360
His verdict?

200
00:05:32,460 --> 00:05:34,440
No skill is future-proof.

201
00:05:34,580 --> 00:05:37,190
And yes, he has a book to sell.

202
00:05:37,650 --> 00:05:39,390
And I just think this

203
00:05:39,430 --> 00:05:41,870
cannot work any longer.

204
00:05:41,910 --> 00:05:44,840
It has reached a dead end.

205
00:05:45,390 --> 00:05:46,350
His warning comes

206
00:05:46,390 --> 00:05:47,900
from his own country.

207
00:05:48,130 --> 00:05:49,670
More than ten years ago,

208
00:05:49,710 --> 00:05:50,970
England made coding,

209
00:05:51,010 --> 00:05:52,180
the skill of the future,

210
00:05:52,220 --> 00:05:53,650
a required school

211
00:05:53,690 --> 00:05:55,450
subject from age five.

212
00:05:55,810 --> 00:05:57,560
Today, writing code is one

213
00:05:57,600 --> 00:05:58,470
of the things these

214
00:05:58,510 --> 00:06:00,080
machines do best.

215
00:06:00,320 --> 00:06:03,080
So betting on one job has a catch.

216
00:06:03,250 --> 00:06:04,490
You only find out if you

217
00:06:04,530 --> 00:06:06,660
won when childhood is over.

218
00:06:06,920 --> 00:06:08,260
But there is a clue.

219
00:06:08,530 --> 00:06:09,530
Take a guess.

220
00:06:09,690 --> 00:06:11,510
Which job is America expected

221
00:06:11,550 --> 00:06:14,220
