233
00:06:32,310 --> 00:06:33,310
there is work where we'll

234
00:06:33,350 --> 00:06:34,850
still want a person.

235
00:06:35,090 --> 00:06:36,150
At a bedside.

236
00:06:36,280 --> 00:06:37,290
In a classroom.

237
00:06:37,500 --> 00:06:38,540
Honestly, though?

238
00:06:38,870 --> 00:06:40,040
Home care pays about

239
00:06:40,080 --> 00:06:42,090
$36,000 a year,

240
00:06:42,130 --> 00:06:43,900
and nothing guarantees more.

241
00:06:44,460 --> 00:06:45,330
So here's what

242
00:06:45,370 --> 00:06:46,830
the evidence supports.

243
00:06:47,100 --> 00:06:49,370
The biggest job growth is in care,

244
00:06:49,410 --> 00:06:51,140
where a human is the point.

245
00:06:51,580 --> 00:06:52,470
Whether we pay it what

246
00:06:52,510 --> 00:06:54,310
it's worth is up to us.

247
00:06:54,520 --> 00:06:55,800
But if machines carry

248
00:06:55,840 --> 00:06:57,730
