295
00:08:10,180 --> 00:08:11,030
It's decided at

296
00:08:11,070 --> 00:08:12,410
your kitchen table.

297
00:08:13,500 --> 00:08:15,130
So what does a parent do

298
00:08:15,170 --> 00:08:16,860
there, starting tonight?

299
00:08:17,230 --> 00:08:18,830
Start with the six-year-old.

300
00:08:19,020 --> 00:08:20,730
Use these machines together.

301
00:08:20,980 --> 00:08:21,730
Ask where the answer

302
00:08:21,770 --> 00:08:22,770
could be wrong.

303
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:24,290
Susskind borrows a rule

304
00:08:24,330 --> 00:08:24,880
from the old

305
00:08:24,920 --> 00:08:26,990
fight over calculators in school.

306
00:08:27,230 --> 00:08:28,230
Teach both.

307
00:08:28,280 --> 00:08:29,240
Test both.

308
00:08:29,280 --> 00:08:31,110
With the machine, and without it.

309
00:08:31,230 --> 00:08:32,890
Most schools aren't there yet.

310
00:08:33,050 --> 00:08:34,580
Your kitchen table can be.

311
00:08:35,130 --> 00:08:36,570
Doing both guards against

312
00:08:36,610 --> 00:08:38,300
a child who can't think without

313
00:08:38,340 --> 00:08:40,450
the machine, and a child who

314
00:08:40,490 --> 00:08:42,750
uses it alone, in secret.

315
00:08:43,130 --> 00:08:44,620
Most American teenagers

316
00:08:44,660 --> 00:08:46,440
already use chatbots.

317
00:08:46,650 --> 00:08:48,280
Only about half of their parents

318
00:08:48,320 --> 00:08:49,810
think their own kid does.

319
00:08:50,250 --> 00:08:51,000
When your child

320
00:08:51,040 --> 00:08:52,330
asks you something,

321
00:08:52,370 --> 00:08:54,390
don't always hand over the answer.

322
00:08:54,610 --> 00:08:55,610
Ask back.

323
00:08:55,880 --> 00:08:56,780
It protects against

324
00:08:56,820 --> 00:08:58,530
a quiet kind of failure.

325
00:08:58,890 --> 00:09:00,360
Every answer in reach,

326
00:09:00,430 --> 00:09:01,750
and no questions.

327
00:09:02,350 --> 00:09:03,730
For the twelve-year-old,

328
00:09:03,890 --> 00:09:06,460
protect the slow, human things.

329
00:09:06,650 --> 00:09:07,780
Real friends.

330
00:09:07,820 --> 00:09:09,160
Real arguments.

331
00:09:09,320 --> 00:09:10,370
A chore that somebody

332
00:09:10,410 --> 00:09:11,470
is counting on.

333
00:09:11,710 --> 00:09:12,670
That's the counterweight

334
00:09:12,710 --> 00:09:13,550
to a companion

335
00:09:13,590 --> 00:09:14,730
that is always there

336
00:09:14,770 --> 00:09:16,670
and never needs anything back.

337
00:09:17,030 --> 00:09:18,660
And for the eighteen-year-old,

338
00:09:18,810 --> 00:09:21,330
stop steering toward one job.

339
00:09:21,580 --> 00:09:22,840
Susskind has a different

340
00:09:22,880 --> 00:09:24,590
question for the dinner table.

341
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:27,340
And so I say,

342
00:09:27,380 --> 00:09:28,260
you know, ask, you know,

343
00:09:28,300 --> 00:09:29,100
what sort of problems

344
00:09:29,140 --> 00:09:30,360
you want to spend your life

345
00:09:30,400 --> 00:09:32,040
solving, your career solving,

346
00:09:32,080 --> 00:09:33,160
rather than what particular

347
00:09:33,200 --> 00:09:34,200
job you want to do.

348
00:09:34,680 --> 00:09:37,100
Problems, not job titles.

349
00:09:37,380 --> 00:09:38,360
That saves a child

350
00:09:38,400 --> 00:09:39,560
from years spent

351
00:09:39,600 --> 00:09:40,590
chasing a job that's

352
00:09:40,630 --> 00:09:42,270
gone by graduation.

353
00:09:42,500 --> 00:09:44,170
None of it is guaranteed.

354
00:09:44,490 --> 00:09:45,790
But look at that list.

355
00:09:45,930 --> 00:09:47,550
There isn't a job on it.

356
00:09:47,860 --> 00:09:49,030
Every line describes

357
00:09:49,070 --> 00:09:50,540
a kind of person.

358
00:09:50,870 --> 00:09:52,060
One who asks.

359
00:09:52,130 --> 00:09:53,300
One who shows up.

360
00:09:53,580 --> 00:09:55,280
One with a problem to solve.

361
00:09:56,420 --> 00:09:58,180
And at your kitchen table,

362
00:09:58,220 --> 00:10:00,110
your child is still waiting.

363
00:10:00,550 --> 00:10:02,520
"What should I be when I grow up?"

364
00:10:03,550 --> 00:10:05,170
You don't have to know what.

365
00:10:05,400 --> 00:10:06,920
You can help with who.

366
00:10:07,260 --> 00:10:08,660
Your parents didn't raise you

367
00:10:08,700 --> 00:10:10,500
to compete with electricity.

368
00:10:10,810 --> 00:10:12,790
They tried to raise a good person.

369
00:10:13,150 --> 00:10:13,950
Your kids won't

370
00:10:13,990 --> 00:10:16,030
compete with superintelligence.

371
00:10:16,160 --> 00:10:17,370
They'll grow up with it.

372
00:10:17,830 --> 00:10:19,050
What matters is who

373
00:10:19,090 --> 00:10:20,460
they grow up to be.

374
00:10:21,560 --> 00:10:23,380
That's what this channel is for:

375
00:10:23,470 --> 00:10:25,130
making sure superintelligence

376
00:10:25,170 --> 00:10:26,960
goes well for everybody.

377
00:10:27,170 --> 00:10:27,930
And first of all

378
00:10:27,970 --> 00:10:29,820
for the children born into it.

379
00:10:30,120 --> 00:10:31,120
Want that too?

380
00:10:31,220 --> 00:10:32,220
Then subscribe.

